        "The definition’s first claim—\"Skin is the part of the body that, when exposed to sunlight, helps produce vitamin D\"—includes a general anatomical description of skin that is not provided in the packet text. The packet only mentions that the body produces vitamin D when exposed to sunlight on the skin, without defining skin itself.",
        "The portion about reduced daylight in winter lowering vitamin D levels and further reducing serotonin activity is supported, but the overall definition is not, because the unsupported general statement about what skin is is substantive."
